flowchart TD
    A["POST /api/recommendations/generate/{vulnerability_id}"] --> B[Load stored vulnerability]
    B -->|Missing| C[Return 404 vulnerability not found]
    B -->|Found| D[Build context from host, port, service,<br/>severity, type and description]

    D --> E{Local Ollama provider configured?}
    E -->|Yes| F[Request up to three evidence-only suggestions]
    E -->|No| G[Return 201 with an empty recommendation collection]
    F --> H{Usable Ollama output returned?}
    H -->|No| G
    H -->|Yes| I[Filter output through safety and scope rules]
    I --> J{Output accepted?}
    J -->|No| G
    J -->|Yes| K[Format risk, priority, likelihood,<br/>impact, confidence and manual steps]
    K --> L[Persist recommendation with PENDING_APPROVAL status]
    L --> M[(recommendations table)]
    M --> N[Return 201 recommendation collection]

    CA["CLI: ./ptas.sh recommend --scan-id ID --all"] --> CB[Load every stored finding for the scan]
    CB --> CC[Skip findings already covered by an active validated Ollama recommendation]
    CC --> CD{Any uncovered findings?}
    CD -->|No| CM[Display genuine coverage and any missing finding IDs]
    CD -->|Yes| CE[Split uncovered findings into small batches]
    CE --> CF[Request strict JSON from local Ollama<br/>with one item for each finding ID]
    CF --> CG{Model response available?}
    CG -->|No| CL[Keep finding uncovered and display safe failure]
    CG -->|Yes| CH[Validate finding ID, exact target,<br/>tool allowlist, safety and service port]
    CH --> CI{Recommendation accepted?}
    CI -->|No| CL
    CI -->|Yes| CJ[Persist as realtime-ollama<br/>with PENDING_APPROVAL status]
    CJ --> CK{More batches in this run?}
    CL --> CK
    CK -->|Yes| CE
    CK -->|No| CM[Display genuine coverage and any missing finding IDs]

    NOTE[There is no static or rule-based recommendation fallback.<br/>Recommendations remain advisory and PTAS never executes them.]
    NOTE -.-> G
    NOTE -.-> CH
